  "body": "**What happens:** `mark_law::budget_of` declares a mark for an Engrave or Trace, and `stock_sim::credit_marks` credits that budget against every part the setup holds (`setup_align::parts_facets_in`). A part-source mark on part B whose flank enters a neighbouring part A by its depth is therefore credited on A too and passes the program sim.\n\nMeasured on #1621's probe (B the #1585 pocket block on x [0, 40], A a 40 x 40 x 8 box on x [-40, -0.7], 80 x 80 x 8 stock, EM-0600-4FL): a 0.3 mm Trace / Engrave round B, its flank 2.3 mm x 0.3 mm into A, **posted on the aligned stock** before #1621.\n\n**Why it is P7, not P1:** since #1621 (PR #1622) the operation itself judges A with the plain solid law (no budget) and refuses the cut on both stocks, so no wrong program posts. The two judges disagree only in the sim's direction (looser) on a neighbour.\n\n**Expected:** the sim credits a mark only on the part(s) the operation marks (its source's entities for a part source; every part for a stock source, where the op's own law reads them all), so the sim agrees with the op.\n\n**Where:** `crates/app/src/stock_sim_marks.rs`, `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/mark.rs` (`credit_marks`), `crates/app/src/operation/mark_law.rs` (`budget_of`).\n\nFound while fixing #1621 (PR #1622; `docs/decisions/1607-stock-source-law.md`, #1621 section).\n\nDone means: the #1621 probe with the op's neighbour law disabled is refused by the program sim on the aligned stock; a legal mark on B still posts; pinned and mutation-checked.\n",
